Strip metadata using mat2 / exiftool.

The cleaned copy is written to <path>.stripped unless --output-file
is given. Runs in server mode if --server / $USULNET_API_URL is
set, otherwise against the local Docker daemon.

A short summary line ("stripped: <input> -> <output> (<bytes>)") is
printed on success.

Usage:
  usulnet meta strip <path> [flags]

Examples:
  usulnet meta strip photo.jpg
  usulnet meta strip photo.jpg -o cleaned.jpg
  usulnet meta strip doc.pdf --server https://usulnet.local

Flags:
  -h, --help                 help for strip
  -o, --output-file string   output path for cleaned file (default <input>.stripped)

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string    config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --image string     toolkit image (local mode only; default $USULNET_RECON_TOOLKIT_IMAGE)
      --json             shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string    output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet            suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)
      --server string    usulnet API URL (forces server mode; default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --timeout string   container timeout (e.g. 30s)
      --token string     API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)
